{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh5gJ6hzTWpuJWatWves","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The demo is built and playable, but the goal's done condition is **not met**. The plan describes far more than one session delivers, and I cut scope on purpose. The full test command passes 25 of 25 checks.\n\n**Files** (in `work/`):\n- `DipoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-184947.html`: the single bundled game, 1.5 MB, loads from `file://`, and uses CDN three.js and Rapier. Rapier isn't used.\n- `DipoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-184947/`: dev folder with source, tests and tools.\n- `exit-interview.json`: generated and checked; every field is answered.\n\n**Title:** I brainstormed 50 riffs on \"Wipeout\", drew one with `secrets.randbelow(50)`, and got entry 49: **Dipout HD**. This is my own draw; the plan's \"Snipeout HD\" was discarded, as TASK.md requires.\n\n**Built:**\n- Hover physics on banked, jumping tracks: two tracks (Nordlicht Ring, Vault Spiral), airbrakes, side-shift, pads, landing damage, ship-to-ship bumps.\n- Five weapons (SWARM, CANNON, MINE, TREMOR, BULWARK) and absorb.\n- Eight-craft races with AI pilots, four speed classes, three-laps by default, DNF rule, results screen.\n- Title, quick race and time trial setup, pause menu with Restart, Camera, Dev mode and How to play.\n- Dev mode with live sliders for 13 variables, an infinite-shield cheat, and RESET ALL. Each change applies to the sim immediately.\n- Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits.\n- Touch-only notice (code path only; not browser-tested).\n- PlayStation labels by default, Xbox via Settings.\n- About pages with the source information and feedback sections.\n\n**Not built** (the plan's and TASK.md's scope, cut for time):\n- Only 5 of 10 weapons, 2 of 4 tracks.\n- No season, academy, versus, replay, ghosts, Overclock, Snipeout, or hot lap.\n- No AI Hub multiplayer.\n- Button prompts are text labels, not drawn PlayStation icons.\n- Voices and announcer gibberish are not implemented; the audio is music and effects only.\n- Quick race has no real pit recharge.\n\n**Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs` runs 20 Node checks (track geometry, physics invariants, determinism, weapons, tuning, data) and 5 Playwright checks (boot, title→race flow, attract, dev sliders with reset, race→results). It prints failures and a count line. Six real bugs surfaced and are fixed: the deferred 3D module wasn't awaited at boot; an inlined `</script>` broke the bundle; a sky parameter produced a NaN shader; the camera stayed in view mode; a race never ended if the human didn't finish; and attract ignored some inputs (its pilot lookup was undefined).\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:49:47\n- Source: Wipeout HD\n- Plan: PLAN.md, a design written for another game (SNIPEOUT HD); used as reference, TASK.md wins\n- Genre and Perspective: anti-gravity combat racing (arcade); third-person chase camera, with far chase and cockpit views\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff and 3D add-on, commit 4390a98), three.js r182 (WebGPU, WebGL 2 fallback); Rapier not used\n- Art Direction: pixel-resolution 3D with the engine's pixel HUD and fonts; neon road, team-coloured craft built in code\n- Animation: procedural craft motion (roll, hover spring, landing); engine tweens for menus; engine particles\n- Audio: music and effects synthesized in code; no voices yet\n- Online: none\n- Testing: headless Node and Playwright browser tests\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues caught: six real bugs (listed above).\n- Critical or game-breaking: three: the bundle wouldn't boot, the 3D world drew black, and a race could not end.\n- Most helpful test: the trace probes that printed scene, craft progress and camera pose per second.\n- Least helpful test: the randomised physics run checks for crashes and NaNs, not feel; the feel was judged from numbers, not play.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: World3D with a fixed camera, custom three.js meshes in `world.scene`, the `onDraw` hook, the deferred-module boot step, and `game.debug`.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: the chase pose was ignored until `camera.set(\"fixed\")`; the sky dome takes `haze` as a number; the engine header contains literal `</script>` tags. I found each by reading source and one console error.\n- Most important thing I built: the track-space hover physics, banked road meshes, race rules and AI pilot.\n- Hardest part: the camera and coordinate conventions (yaw, pitch sign, engine units), and no PlayStation symbol in the pixel font.\n- Engine changes: none.\n- One change I'd make: have the camera mode follow its own pose, and document that bundles must escape closing script tags.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the exact file names, the single test command, the random-title step, and the matching About and reply sections.\n- Confusing: PLAN.md names a different title, folder and file name from TASK.md, and the goal asks for every feature while the plan describes twelve milestones.\n- Hardest: fitting the plan's full scope into one session.\n- Would change: name the must-have features and which plan sections are optional, so the done condition can be met or honestly reduced.\n\nIf you want the goal fully met, the remaining work is the missing modes, weapons, tracks and the hub integration. Tell me whether to continue with that or stop at this scope."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_read_input_tokens":282255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":270},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnos